PART 1 -- END TO END ON A REAL BOOTED KAIROS SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ISO under test: kairos-hadron-v0.5.1-standard-amd64-generic-v4.3.0-85-g96ef1c97d
                -k3sv1.36.4+k3s1.iso
That ISO is built from 96ef1c97d, i.e. the agent shipped inside it IS the
pre-fix ("BASE") build. Hadron is musl, so it is exactly the case #4661
describes. Booted live in QEMU/KVM:

  qemu-system-x86_64 -accel kvm -cpu host -m 4G -smp 4 \
    -kernel <iso:/boot/kernel> -initrd <iso:/boot/initrd> \
    -append 'cdroot root=live:CDLABEL=COS_LIVE rd.live.dir=/ \
             rd.live.squashimg=rootfs.squashfs net.ifnames=1 \
             console=tty1 console=ttyS0 rd.cos.disable vga=795 nomodeset \
             install-mode selinux=0 rd.live.overlay.overlayfs' \
    -drive if=ide,media=cdrom,file=<iso>,readonly=on \
    -netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-pci,netdev=n0 ...

The PR binary (built from a902edec0, sha256
3033937d95355c8d6becd41a4f901d53b0920a048571e82c0a7aef6c657e8db4) was curled
into the running guest and dropped in as /tmp/prbin/kairos-agent, so both
builds ran against the SAME rootfs, kernel and machine.

